 "background": "A lament for lost youth, not for a lover. The singer tells the sun and moon to go dark and calls the forest her sister. The forest's leaves will grow back each spring; her youth never will. It is one of the most performed slow songs in the repertoire, recorded by everyone from Aleksandar Sarievski to Toše Proeski. Qwen's draft adds that it is usually sung as a mother's lament, and that other versions give the reason as wanting her son not to be sent to war (unchecked).",
